# ============================================================================
# SaaSPath — environment variables
# ============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the real values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local        (macOS / Linux)
#   copy .env.example .env.local      (Windows cmd)
#
# `.env.local` is git-ignored and must NEVER be committed.
# ============================================================================


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Supabase — REQUIRED
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where to find them:
#   Supabase Dashboard -> your project -> Project Settings -> API
#
#   * Project URL        -> NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
#   * anon / public key  -> NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#
# Both values are exposed to the browser (the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix inlines them
# into the client bundle). This is safe: access is governed by Row Level
# Security policies defined in supabase/setup.sql.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Supabase — OPTIONAL (server-side admin only)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where to find it:
#   Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API -> service_role key
#
# The service role key BYPASSES Row Level Security. Use it only in trusted
# server-side code (Server Actions, Route Handlers, scripts). NEVER prefix it
# with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and NEVER expose it to the browser.
#
# Leave it commented out unless you actually need admin operations.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Google OAuth — configured in Supabase, not here
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google sign-in is wired through Supabase Auth, so no Google client id/secret
# belongs in this file. Instead, add them once in:
#   Supabase Dashboard -> Authentication -> Providers -> Google
#
# See SETUP.md ("Google OAuth") for the full walkthrough, including the
# Authorized redirect URI that must be registered in Google Cloud Console:
#   https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Cloudflare / OpenNext — no secrets in this file
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The app is deployed to Cloudflare Workers via OpenNext. Runtime secrets are
# stored in Cloudflare, not in `.env.local`:
#
#   npx wrangler secret put NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
#   npx wrangler secret put NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#
# For local previews, OpenNext reads `.dev.vars` (git-ignored). Create it with
# the same keys as above:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key
